Subject: [PATCH 22/22] ttf: a quadratic whose control point is on an end is a
 line

A glyf contour may record an off-curve, an on-curve and an off-curve point at
one place, a corner drawn with straight lines (Kirang Haerang's U+D683,
Single Day, Gothic A1). Read as they are, a later step that merges
coincident points kept an off-curve one, and the corner became a curve. Such
an off-curve point is now dropped, and a quadratic left without one is a
line.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
